<p>
For someone who spends as much time in Emacs as I do, it is faintly ridiculous how much of my configuration time goes on the save keybinding. I have tried the stock chord, a shorter prefix, function keys, and spare keys; each one feels right for a day, and then the search starts again. So I am going to stop optimizing the key and let Emacs save the buffer for me. This post is the setup, not the verdict!
</p>


